; Do NOT set environment/host specific setttings (like registry or script-shell) here. Use ~/.npmrc
;
; Since pnpm 11 only auth and registry settings are read from .npmrc.
; Every other pnpm setting must live in pnpm-workspace.yaml (per repo)
; or ~/.config/pnpm/config.yaml (per machine). https://pnpm.io/settings

; A hoisted node_modules is NOT set here and must not be re-added to this file:
; since pnpm 11 a `node-linker=hoisted` line here is silently ignored, which
; looks like it works. The layout is decided by `nodeLinker` in
; pnpm-workspace.yaml, where it ships commented out.
;
; A per-build `pnpm install --node-linker=hoisted` does NOT work either: pnpm
; verifies the dependency tree before running a script, so the flag survives the
; install and is then relinked back to the layout declared in the repository
; before `pnpm run deploy`. The Windows installer build (which hits MAX_PATH
; while copying the deep .pnpm paths) therefore uncomments the line in
; pnpm-workspace.yaml instead - see the note next to it.
;
; Enabling `nodeLinker: hoisted` for everyone changes resolution for all devs,
; CI and Docker builds and re-exposes phantom dependencies. Cases where hoisting
; has been needed:
; - Solves missing Next.js standalone build dependencies https://github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/48017
; - Solves Next.js standalone build breaking pnpm monorepo dependencies https://github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/65636
; - Solves Turborepo error writing to cache https://github.com/vercel/turbo/issues/6823
